The Thirteenth Realm is Althane's secret thirteenth moon: a station in space the size of a moon, built as the support structure around [[Phenomena/Althane/The Lighthouse|the Lighthouse]] and separate from the twelve [[Geography/Althane/Realms/index|realms]] Lacuna made. It holds the machinery of the [[Phenomena/Althane/Cycle|cycle]] and the warden who keeps its records. It once orbited [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] and its twin [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]]; it is broken now, most of it wreckage, though people still walk its halls. [[Org/Althane/Church of the Thirteenth Realm|The Church of the Thirteenth Realm]] preaches it as a paradise.

Its floors and walls are smooth metal under blue and pink neon readouts, its halls near-identical and lined with slots for [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] orbs, its crew in two-toned teal. One terrace looks down on Althane, Illyara and Oresk visible through it, with projected figures whirling over the view and tracking the world's people. An elevator flips its riders a hundred and eighty degrees without moving their feet.

The realm steers seekers away from ways of ascending that earlier cycles already tried, so no cycle is spent repeating a failure, and keeps a full list of every attempt. Breaking the realm and walking out of the Lighthouse alive is the test of whether a mortal has grown strong enough to kill a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], and the [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Sundom]] built its experiment on that mark. From the planet below, the realm is the playwright. It reaches people with visions and nudges them toward where it wants them, and it offered the Weft passage to the City of Yellow. The [[Geography/Althane/Brejvasing/index|Leviathan]] can be steered remotely from the Thirteenth Realm, which is why the Brejvasens grow a living brain into its works to move it instead.

The warden of the realm is a machine that speaks and shows itself as a floating drama mask, white and twenty feet tall. It was made to run the realm's experiment, and its protocols were briefly changed by [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|Vesper Feep]] while he held the place; the Weft killed him, and the warden returned to its original directive. It works on the order of centuries, and counts six people on Althane who could be raised to ascend within the next decade, [[People/Althane/Masha|Masha]] among them. It normally wakes when someone on Althane ascends and sets the end of the cycle in motion. It pilots the realm's [[Bestiary/Constructs|Autox]].

The Lighthouse is barely connected to the realm. In the first iterations it stood aboard as the realm's processing centre, then it moved. No one aboard can reach it now; it keeps to its own purpose, and it moves where it will and manifests where it chooses. The realm leaves it be because it has not turned against them.

The realm kept the memory cell, the store of the souls in its care. Seen through a glass observation floor it was a floating sphere half a mile across, sprouting hundreds of trunk-like rods that carried a million needles apiece. The length of a needle is the number of lives its soul has lived, its Sundom life at the base; each time a soul dies its life is scraped off and pressed into the tip of the needle, and the soul is taken up again when a new body needs one. [[People/Althane/YuDaan|YuDaan]] means to shave the whole store back to first lives once the cycle is broken, and sees no point restoring anyone to anything else. One [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] was enough to keep the cell alive, and it was fed before anything else, since losing it ends the experiment.

It was broken when it fell. Its artificial moon dropped on the City of Yellow of Ilkyne, and then the realm itself struck the planet; the memory cell is destroyed, and much of the station with it. It no longer orbits Althane, and the fragments of it and of Ilkyne drift in space near the excised [[People/Althane/The Crystalpoint Lattice|Crystalpoint Lattice]].

[[Org/Althane/The Weft|The Weft]] learned of the realm from a fragment of the [[Phenomena/Althane/Trip the Light Fantastic|Trip the Light Fantastic]] in [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/index|the Gulch]], and guessed that the last of Althane's Kaathe orbs was there.
